<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN JUNE HOUSING FINANCE FALLS 2.1 PCT.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN JUNE HOUSING FINANCE FALLS 2.1 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance commitments for owner-occupied housing in Australia fell 2.1 percent by volume to 39,162 dwellings in June from the May level of 39,985, seasonally-adjusted, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In value terms, housing finance rose to A$4.29 billion in June from A$4.25 billion in May, the bureau said.  </p>
<p>Australian housing finance, June 1997 -</p>
<p>    Dwelling commitments	June 97    May 97	June 96</p>
<p>    Seasonally-adjusted	 39,162     39,985	35,712</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		    39,838     41,979	35,520</p>
<p>    Trend			   40,203     40,491	38,200</p>
<p>Value (A$ billion)</p>
<p>    Seasonally-adjusted	  4.29	 4.25	  3.50</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		     4.36	 4.59	  3.52</p>
<p>    Trend estimates		4.33	 4.35	  3.75</p>
<p>NOTE: The bureau said that in adjusted terms decreases were recorded for each type of housing. The number of commitments under new finance but excluding refinancing fell by five percent while refinancing commitments increased by 9.6 percent. It also said trend estimates for total dwellings financed had now shown decreases in the past three months and was down 0.7 percent in June.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
